From: SWEET RMX1971 port (ZCode agent + AppleCampus)
Subject: [PATCH 0089] sweet: framebuffer - static flush buffer, layer/pixel diagnostics

panic27 findings:

  * the "swap record allocation failed" lines were a mis-attached else from
    0087 (it fired on every non-flush vsync, not on ENOMEM). Replace the
    whole per-flush IOMallocData/IOFreeData dance with one static record
    buffer.
  * the heartbeat shows the vsync timer running for the whole session
    (34200 ticks, ~9.5 min), so the freeze was never a dead timer.
  * to tell "the app really is drawing black" from "we copy the wrong
    surface", log skipped layers (no surface / default surface / out of
    bounds) and the centre pixel of what we do copy.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
